From b1957443ed3f9d8c47516f2ad6c88688511adffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:11:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] UFS driver: build prsl with the physics' gas constants

atmos_phys_driver_statein gives the physics the layer pressure
prsl = dm*rTv/dphi with rTv = rdgas*T*(1+zvir*q), using the dycore's
constants. The physics turns prsl back into density with its own con_rd
and con_fvirt (the boundary layer's rho_a, Noah-MP's density). In a 32-bit
build rdgas is single precision (287.04998779 for 287.05), so that density
differs from the layer's actual mass per volume, dm/dphi, by 4.25e-8.

The boundary layer adds evap*del/(g*dz) of water but books evap*rho_a,
which is also what Noah-MP debits from the land: the atmosphere received
4.1e-8 of surface evaporation more than the land lost.

Compute rTv with con_rd and con_fvirt.

Measured with in-model meters (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 32-bit dycore): added
minus booked fell from +4.11e-8 of evaporation (+3.1e-8 kg/m2 per 6 h) to
1.6e-16.
---
 driver/UFS/atmosphere.F90 | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/driver/UFS/atmosphere.F90 b/driver/UFS/atmosphere.F90
index f2654b5..4e6c0ab 100644
--- a/driver/UFS/atmosphere.F90
+++ b/driver/UFS/atmosphere.F90
@@ -155,6 +155,7 @@ use constantsR4_mod,          only: cp_air, rdgas, grav, rvgas, kappa, pstd_mks
 #else
 use constants_mod,          only: cp_air, rdgas, grav, rvgas, kappa, pstd_mks
 #endif
+use physcons,               only: con_rd, con_fvirt
 use time_manager_mod,       only: time_type, get_time, set_time, operator(+), &
                                   operator(-), operator(/), time_type_to_real
 use fms_mod,                only: error_mesg, FATAL,                 &
@@ -2295,7 +2296,8 @@ contains
            rTv = rdgas*IPD_Statein%tgrs(im,k)*virq_max(q_grs(:),q_min)
 #else
            qgrs_rad = max(qmin,IPD_Statein%qgrs(im,k,sphum))
-           rTv = rdgas*IPD_Statein%tgrs(im,k)*(1.+zvir*qgrs_rad)
+           ! the physics' constants: it turns prsl back into density with con_rd
+           rTv = con_rd*IPD_Statein%tgrs(im,k)*(1.+con_fvirt*qgrs_rad)
 #endif
            if ( Atm(mygrid)%flagstruct%hydrostatic .or. Atm(mygrid)%flagstruct%use_hydro_pressure )   &
                 IPD_Statein%phii(im,k+1) = IPD_Statein%phii(im,k) &
-- 
